:[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013Z3fLe9FgMabh233VA2iBN":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework; python3 -c \"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('data/skills.json'))\nwant='frame-orchestration render-architect entity-object-model ecs-runtime gameplay-architect gameplay-systems-toolkit scripting-runtime editor-architect ui-architect audio-architect content-pipeline-architect hot-reload-iteration reflection-metadata world-architect world-data-model spatial-transforms rhi-core gpu-driven-pipeline render-graph-scheduling resource-streaming-architect gpu-memory-resources platform-architect job-system-task-graph input-system network-architect replication physics-architect core-runtime-architect render-2d-vector visual-debugging-tools asset-cook-processors'.split()\nfor s in d['skills']:\n  if s['id'] in want:\n    print('=== ',s['id']);print('purpose:',s['purpose']);print('non:',s['non_responsibilities']);print('exp:',s.get('expertise'));print()\n\"","description":"Print key skill cards"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfXzcLyPjoH2ZtZ8dt4Uc","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7bbd47c-92df-4aeb-bc22-0169fed87684","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:48:55.549Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
{"parentUuid":"f7bbd47c-92df-4aeb-bc22-0169fed87684","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"ae46b4cd829201079","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Z3fLe9FgMabh233VA2iBN","type":"tool_result","content":"===  hot-reload-iteration\npurpose: Owns the reload protocol (change detection, dependency invalidation, state preservation) that assets, shaders, scripts, config and C++ live coding plug into; measures edit → see latency.\nnon: [[\"Each system's own reload implementation\", 'resource-streaming-architect'], ['Build system', 'build-system-toolchains']]\nexp: ['live coding', 'state migration', 'iteration-time measurement']\n\n===  core-runtime-architect\npurpose: Core runtime architecture: layering within core, module system and engine lifecycle (parallel boot, init graph, shutdown), configuration and cvars, error-handling and failure model, language and compiler feature policy.\nnon: [['Allocator design', 'memory-allocators'], ['Scheduler', 'job-system-task-graph'], ['Frame loop', 'frame-orchestration']]\nexp: ['C++20/23', 'module systems', 'error models', 'configuration systems']\n\n===  job-system-task-graph\npurpose: Task-parallel execution: work-stealing scheduler, dependency task graphs, fibers and C++20 coroutines, priorities and QoS, heterogeneous-core and NUMA placement, IO/GPU completion integration, parallel algorithms, blocking policy.\nnon: [['Frame phase layout', 'frame-orchestration'], ['IO backends', 'async-io-storage']]\nexp: ['work stealing', 'fibers', 'coroutines', 'hybrid CPU scheduling']\n\n===  frame-orchestration\npurpose: The engine loop expressed as a task graph: frame pipelining across simulation, render and GPU, tick phases and sync points, fixed-step simulation with interpolation, time domains, latency and pacing control.\nnon: [['System ordering inside a phase', 'ecs-runtime'], ['Swapchain presentation', 'rhi-core']]\nexp: ['frame pipelining', 'latency analysis', 'fixed timestep']\n\n===  entity-object-model\npurpose: Object-model strategy and identity: generational entity IDs, stable GUIDs, hard/soft/weak references, the hybrid-model policy stating which data lives in ECS vs services vs asset objects vs UI, events and messaging.\nnon: [['ECS storage and queries', 'ecs-runtime'], ['Asset references', 'content-pipeline-architect'], ['Network IDs', 'replication']]\nexp: ['object models', 'handle systems', 'lifetime design']\n\n===  ecs-runtime\npurpose: ECS: storage (archetype chunks or sparse sets, chosen by ADR), queries, change detection, structural changes and command buffers, system scheduling with access-conflict analysis, relationships, singletons, authoring → runtime baking, debugging.\nnon: [['World partition', 'world-architect'], ['Transform propagation', 'spatial-transforms'], ['Object-model policy', 'entity-object-model']]\nexp: ['ECS architectures', 'data-oriented design', 'parallel scheduling']\n\n===  reflection-metadata\npurpose: Type registry, reflection generation (codegen now, C++26 static reflection when toolchains allow), attributes, the property system, script-binding substrate, dynamic invocation.\nnon: [['Serialization formats', 'serialization-schema'], ['Editor widgets', 'editor-ui-framework'], ['Script VM', 'scripting-runtime']]\nexp: ['metaprogramming', 'code generation', 'C++26 reflection']\n\n===  platform-architect\npurpose: Platform abstraction layer and porting strategy: OS services, CPU/GPU capability discovery, windowing, process lifecycle, capability tiers, and evaluation of new targets (web, cloud streaming).\nnon: [['Graphics API backends', 'rhi-core'], ['Store and online services', 'platform-online-services'], ['Toolchains', 'build-system-toolchains']]\nexp: ['OS internals (Windows, Linux, macOS)', 'porting', 'CPU topology']\n\n===  input-system\npurpose: Action-level input: mapping and context stacks, rebinding, buffering and latency accounting, local-multiplayer assignment, accessibility input options, UI navigation routing, per-device glyphs, recording and replay.\nnon: [['Device drivers and haptics', 'input-devices-haptics'], ['UI focus logic', 'ui-architect']]\nexp: ['input systems', 'latency measurement', 'remapping UX']\n\n===  content-pipeline-architect\npurpose: Asset identity and the content pipeline: asset registry and dependency graph, deterministic incremental per-platform cooking, the cook-step contract, derived-data cache and content-addressed store, distributed cooking, content validation.\nnon: [['Format-specific builders (shaders, animation, clusters…)', 'shader-system'], ['Runtime loading', 'resource-streaming-architect'], ['Import formats', 'asset-import-interchange']]\nexp: ['build systems for data', 'content-addressed storage', 'incremental computation']\n\n===  asset-cook-processors\npurpose: Generic processors: texture processing and GPU texture-compression encoding, mesh optimization, hosting of collision and other domain builders under the cook contract.\nnon: [['Cluster DAG building', 'virtualized-geometry-lod'], ['Animation compression', 'animation-runtime'], ['Shader compilation', 'shader-system']]\nexp: ['BCn/ASTC encoders', 'mesh optimization', 'image processing']\n\n===  resource-streaming-architect\npurpose: Runtime resource model: handles and explicit lifetime, load requests with priority and deadline, dependency-aware loading, the streaming manager (budgets, eviction, prediction), fallbacks, no-stall loading.\nnon: [['IO backends', 'async-io-storage'], ['Package format', 'package-formats-vfs'], ['Texture-specific streaming', 'texture-streaming-vt']]\nexp: ['streaming systems', 'cache eviction', 'async loading']\n\n===  world-architect\npurpose: World representation strategy (data-oriented, no universal scene graph), partitioning and streaming cells, streaming sources, HLOD strategy, simulation LOD and significance, large-world coordinate policy, level transitions, server-side world streaming.\nnon: [['World document format', 'world-data-model'], ['Transform math', 'spatial-transforms'], ['HLOD mesh generation', 'virtualized-geometry-lod']]\nexp: ['open-world streaming', 'spatial partitioning', 'significance systems']\n\n===  world-data-model\npurpose: World and level documents, prefabs with nested overrides and variants, data layers, one-file-per-object layout for collaboration, level instances.\nnon: [['Serialization mechanics', 'serialization-schema'], ['Source-control workflows', 'collaboration-version-control']]\nexp: ['prefab systems', 'override resolution', 'mergeable data design']\n\n===  spatial-transforms\npurpose: Transform representation and parallel hierarchy propagation, attachments, large-world coordinates implementation, generic spatial index and query service for non-physics consumers, spatial hashing.\nnon: [['Physics broadphase', 'collision-detection'], ['GPU culling', 'gpu-driven-pipeline']]\nexp: ['transform hierarchies', 'BVH/grids', 'precision management']\n\n===  render-architect\npurpose: Rendering architecture: pipeline organization, shading-path choice (forward+, deferred, visibility buffer), render-feature contract, render scene and world→render sync, scalability tiers from 2D mobile to path-traced, multi-view, debug modes, render threading.\nnon: [['API backends', 'rhi-core'], ['Pass scheduling', 'render-graph-scheduling'], ['Individual features (GI, shadows…)', 'global-illumination']]\nexp: ['real-time rendering architecture', 'GPU-driven pipelines', 'scalability']\n\n===  rhi-core\npurpose: Render hardware interface over D3D12, Vulkan, Metal, console APIs and WebGPU: queues and command recording, synchronization, bindless descriptors, PSOs and PSO caching, presentation, capability tiers, GPU crash breadcrumbs, driver workarounds.\nnon: [['GPU memory allocation', 'gpu-memory-resources'], ['Barrier planning', 'render-graph-scheduling'], ['Shader compilation', 'shader-system']]\nexp: ['D3D12', 'Vulkan', 'Metal', 'GPU synchronization']\n\n===  gpu-memory-resources\npurpose: GPU heaps and suballocation, residency and overcommit, upload/readback rings, sparse/reserved resources, GPU memory budgeting and defragmentation, lifetimes decoupled from frame boundaries.\nnon: [['Transient aliasing plans', 'render-graph-scheduling'], ['Texture streaming policy', 'texture-streaming-vt']]\nexp: ['D3D12MA/VMA-class allocators', 'residency', 'sparse resources']\n\n===  render-graph-scheduling\npurpose: Render graph declaration and compilation, automatic barriers, transient aliasing, async compute and multi-queue scheduling, TBDR pass merging, history resources, work-graph integration, general GPU compute, readback contract.\nnon: [['Heap allocation', 'gpu-memory-resources'], ['Feature passes', 'render-architect']]\nexp: ['frame graphs', 'GPU scheduling', 'work graphs']\n\n===  gpu-driven-pipeline\npurpose: GPU scene and instance data, GPU frustum and two-phase occlusion culling, indirect and device-generated commands, mesh/amplification shaders, visibility-buffer rasterization, instancing, CPU-driven fallback for low-tier GPUs.\nnon: [['Cluster LOD', 'virtualized-geometry-lod'], ['Render-scene contract', 'render-architect']]\nexp: ['GPU culling', 'mesh shaders', 'ExecuteIndirect']\n\n===  render-2d-vector\npurpose: 2D draw backend shared by 2D games, UI and debug overlays: sprites, tilemaps, 2D lighting, vector paths, UI batching/clipping/SDF, HDR compositing, pixel-perfect modes.\nnon: [['Widget model', 'ui-architect'], ['Glyph shaping', 'text-fonts']]\nexp: ['2D batching', 'vector rasterization', 'SDF rendering']\n\n===  physics-architect\npurpose: Physics architecture: build vs integrate decision, physics world representation and ECS integration, stepping and frame sync, determinism levels, physics LOD, materials, GPU offload evaluation; covers both 2D and 3D.\nnon: [['Collision algorithms', 'collision-detection'], ['Solvers', 'rigid-body-dynamics'], ['Networked physics', 'prediction-rollback']]\nexp: ['physics engines (Jolt, PhysX, Havok, Box2D)', 'simulation architecture']\n\n===  audio-architect\npurpose: Audio engine architecture and threading, device backends, voice management and virtualization, middleware decision, audio budgets.\nnon: [['DSP algorithms', 'audio-dsp-mixing'], ['Spatialization', 'spatial-audio-acoustics']]\nexp: ['real-time audio', 'lock-free audio threads', 'Wwise/FMOD']\n\n===  network-architect\npurpose: Netcode model per game type (authoritative server, lockstep, rollback, P2P/relay), network tick and time, authority model, budgets and scale targets, protocol versioning, sharded worlds evaluation.\nnon: [['Transport', 'network-transport'], ['Replication mechanics', 'replication'], ['Matchmaking services', 'platform-online-services']]\nexp: ['netcode architectures', 'distributed systems', 'latency hiding']\n\n===  replication\npurpose: Entity and property replication, delta compression and quantization, interest management, prioritization, RPCs, snapshot interpolation, replay recording, network ID mapping.\nnon: [['Prediction', 'prediction-rollback'], ['Transport', 'network-transport']]\nexp: ['state synchronization', 'bit packing', 'interest management']\n\n===  gameplay-architect\npurpose: Gameplay framework: rules, players and possession, extension points and game-module structure, game flow and transitions, local players.\nnon: [['Abilities/tags/camera toolkit', 'gameplay-systems-toolkit'], ['Scripting VM', 'scripting-runtime'], ['Game-specific code (the game team)', 'engine-architect']]\nexp: ['gameplay frameworks', 'game architecture']\n\n===  gameplay-systems-toolkit\npurpose: Reusable gameplay systems: abilities, effects and attributes, gameplay tags, camera system, spawning and pooling, gameplay message routing, photo mode.\nnon: [['Generic events', 'entity-object-model'], ['Cinematic cameras', 'cinematics-sequencer']]\nexp: ['ability systems', 'camera design', 'gameplay tags']\n\n===  scripting-runtime\npurpose: Scripting language selection, VM embedding and bindings, sandboxing, debugging and profiling, hot reload, visual scripting, AOT/JIT constraints, GC policy.\nnon: [['Reflection substrate', 'reflection-metadata'], ['Graph editor UI', 'graph-editor-framework']]\nexp: ['VM embedding (Luau, .NET, Wasm)', 'DAP', 'sandboxing']\n\n===  ui-architect\npurpose: UI architecture (retained with data binding for game UI, immediate for developer UI), layout, styling, focus and navigation, animation, in-world UI, designer tool logic, UI performance.\nnon: [['UI draw backend', 'render-2d-vector'], ['Text shaping', 'text-fonts'], ['Editor panels', 'editor-ui-framework']]\nexp: ['UI frameworks', 'layout algorithms', 'MVVM']\n\n===  editor-architect\npurpose: Editor architecture: process model (in- vs out-of-process runtime), editor/runtime data separation, transactions and undo/redo, selection, extension API and tool scripting, play-in-editor isolation, remote live editing, headless editor, large-project performance.\nnon: [['Panels and inspectors', 'editor-ui-framework'], ['World viewport tools', 'world-editor-viewport'], ['Source control', 'collaboration-version-control']]\nexp: ['editor architecture', 'command pattern', 'tool UX']\n\n===  visual-debugging-tools\npurpose: Debug draw API, in-game console and cheats, runtime entity inspector and gameplay debugger, visual logger and rewind, debug menus and overlays.\nnon: [['Logging and traces', 'observability-telemetry'], ['Render buffer visualization', 'render-architect']]\nexp: ['debug tooling', 'visual logging']","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9e81b8c3-be51-4178-93d8-261e5e69cd14","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:48:55.659Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f7bbd47c-92df-4aeb-bc22-0169fed87684","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
